d":"/cluster","page_id":"/cluster","type":"page","content":"Sandbox cluster","breadcrumbs":["DAIMON","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/cluster"},"2":{"id":"/cluster-0","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster","content":"Scheduler in front, manager containers, and nsjail sandboxes built inside each manager — not extra Docker containers."},"3":{"id":"/cluster-1","page_id":"/cluster","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"Architecture"},"4":{"id":"/cluster-2","page_id":"/cluster","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cluster#start","content":"Start"},"5":{"id":"/cluster-3","page_id":"/cluster","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cluster#create-a-sandbox-then-connect-mcp","content":"Create a sandbox, then connect MCP"},"6":{"id":"/cluster-4","page_id":"/cluster","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cluster#reach-sandboxes-from-your-lan","content":"Reach sandboxes from your LAN"},"7":{"id":"/cluster-5","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster","content":"Use this when you want a **fleet of isolated workspaces**, not MCP on the host itself."},"8":{"id":"/cluster-6","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster","content":"A sandbox is **not** a Docker container. It is an nsjail jail **inside** a manager container. You cannot point Claude Code or Cursor at the scheduler (or manager) `/mcp` — that path does not exist. Create a sandbox first, then connect MCP to the returned `mcp_url`."},"9":{"id":"/cluster-7","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"Layer"},"10":{"id":"/cluster-8","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"What it is"},"11":{"id":"/cluster-9","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"What it is not"},"12":{"id":"/cluster-10","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"**Scheduler**"},"13":{"id":"/cluster-11","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"HTTP front on `:18081`. Same API as a manager. Discovers manager nodes, places new sandboxes, and routes later calls using a signed sandbox id."},"14":{"id":"/cluster-12","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"Not a sandbox runtime. Does not run `processd-mcp`. Has no `/mcp`."},"15":{"id":"/cluster-13","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"**Manager container**"},"16":{"id":"/cluster-14","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"One Docker/K8s container running `processd-sandbox-manager`. Image also ships `nsjail`, `pasta`, `processd-scheduler`, and the `processd-mcp` binary."},"17":{"id":"/cluster-15","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"Not one-container-per-agent. Not an MCP server you connect a client to."},"18":{"id":"/cluster-16","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"**Sandbox**"},"19":{"id":"/cluster-17","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"Created **inside** that manager on `POST /sandboxes`: nsjail namespaces + cgroup, a `processd-mcp` worker, a workspace. MCP is proxied as `http://<scheduler>/sandboxes/<id>/mcp`."},"20":{"id":"/cluster-18","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"Not a new Docker container. No Docker socket."},"21":{"id":"/cluster-19","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"Store sandbox ids **opaque** — they encode which manager owns the jail."},"22":{"id":"/cluster-20","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#architecture","content":"You need Docker with **cgroup v2** writable. Linux hosts work; Docker Desktop for macOS cannot use `network_mode: host`."},"23":{"id":"/clu