it while the client is connected."},"30":{"id":"/cluster-28","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#create-a-sandbox-then-connect-mcp","content":"`mcp_url` looks like `http://127.0.0.1:18081/sandboxes/<id>/mcp`. Paste it into Claude Code (`.mcp.json`) or Cursor:"},"31":{"id":"/cluster-29","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#create-a-sandbox-then-connect-mcp","content":"Use the **sandbox** token, not a manager token. For text-only clients, append `/text-only` to the path (`.../mcp/text-only`). Full client notes: Connect."},"32":{"id":"/cluster-30","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#create-a-sandbox-then-connect-mcp","content":"To drive the sandbox from Python instead of an MCP client, keep the SDK session:"},"33":{"id":"/cluster-31","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#create-a-sandbox-then-connect-mcp","content":"That context manager already talks MCP for you and deletes the sandbox on exit."},"34":{"id":"/cluster-32","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#reach-sandboxes-from-your-lan","content":"Set `public_base_url` in `scheduler-config.local.yaml` to the host's real LAN IP (or Tailscale IP). **Do not** use `0.0.0.0` in URLs you hand to clients."},"35":{"id":"/cluster-33","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#reach-sandboxes-from-your-lan","content":"Then recreate with the same overlay:"},"36":{"id":"/cluster-34","page_id":"/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cluster#reach-sandboxes-from-your-lan","content":"Manager env vars: Configuration."},"37":{"id":"/connect","page_id":"/connect","type":"page","content":"Connect","breadcrumbs":["DAIMON","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/connect"},"38":{"id":"/connect-0","page_id":"/connect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/connect","content":"Point Claude Code, Cursor, or any HTTP MCP client at processd-mcp."},"39":{"id":"/connect-1","page_id":"/connect","type":"heading","tags":[],"url"