s by pattern; search contents with ripgrep."},"111":{"id":"/-17","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#core-mcp-tools","content":"`WebFetch`"},"112":{"id":"/-18","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#core-mcp-tools","content":"Fetch a URL through the sandbox instead of shell `curl`."},"113":{"id":"/-19","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#core-mcp-tools","content":"`exec_command` / `write_stdin`"},"114":{"id":"/-20","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#core-mcp-tools","content":"Interactive PTY session when you need a real TTY."},"115":{"id":"/-21","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#core-mcp-tools","content":"`GetRuntimeContext`"},"116":{"id":"/-22","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#core-mcp-tools","content":"Workdir, filesystem/network policy, and tool capabilities."},"117":{"id":"/-23","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#core-mcp-tools","content":"Clients send `X-Access-Token`. `/health` is unauthenticated."},"118":{"id":"/-24","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#tutorials","content":"<Card title=\"Linux binary\" href=\"/terminal\" description=\"Static musl binary on any Linux. One-liner installer is Debian/Ubuntu + systemd. Put Tailscale in front — MCP is not encrypted.\" />"},"119":{"id":"/-25","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#tutorials","content":"<Card title=\"Sandbox cluster\" href=\"/cluster\" description=\"Scheduler in front, manager containers, nsjail sandboxes built inside each manager.\" />"},"120":{"id":"/-26","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#tutorials","content":"<Card title=\"macOS app\" href=\"/desktop\" description=\"Launch the desktop app, edit policy visually, run the kernel locally.\" />"},"121":{"id":"/-27","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#tutorials","content":"<Card title=\"Connect\" href=\"/connect\" description=\"Claude Code, Cursor, or the SDK: URL + X-Access-Token.\" />"},"122":{"id":"/-28","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#tutorials","content":"<Card title=\"Configuration\" href=\"/config\" description=\"Environment file and sandbox-policy.yaml: host, token, paths, network.\" />"},"123":{"id":"/-29","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#tutorials","content":"Assets come from daimon-hq/release **latest**. A new `core-v*` or `gui-v*` tag updates what the install commands download."},"124":{"id":"/terminal","page_id":"/terminal","type":"page","content":"Linux binary","breadcrumbs":["DAIMON","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/terminal"},"125":{"id":"/terminal-0","page_id":"/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/terminal","content":"Static musl processd-mcp for any Linux amd64/arm64. The one-liner installer is Debian/Ubuntu + systemd."},"126":{"id":"/terminal-1","page_id":"/terminal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/terminal#install-debian--ubuntu","content":"Install (Debian / Ubuntu)"},"127":{"id":"/terminal-2","page_id":"/terminal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/terminal#other-linux","content":"Other Linux"},"128":{"id":"/terminal-3","page_id":"/terminal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/terminal#no-tls--use-tailscale","content":"No TLS — use Tailscale"},"129":{"id":"/terminal-4","page_id":"/terminal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/terminal#upgrade-and-uninstall","content":"Upgrade and uninstall"},"130":{"id":"/terminal-5","page_id":"/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/terminal","content":"Use this when you already have a Linux server and want an MCP client to drive **that host's** terminal. No Docker."},"131":{"id":"/terminal-6","page_id":"/terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/terminal","content":"The release binary is **static musl** (`processd-mcp-linux-amd64` / `processd-mcp-linux-arm64`). It does not link glibc, so it runs on generic Linux. The **install script** is the Debian/Ubuntu path: it needs `systemd`, writes a unit under `/etc/systemd/system`, and uses `apt`-style host layout."},"132":{"id":"/terminal-7","page_id":"/termin